==English==
{{Webster 1913}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|simplicite}}, from {{der|en|fro|simplicite}}, from {{der|en|la|simplicitās}}, from {{m|la|simplex||simple}}. See {{m|en|simple}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/sɪmˈplɪsɪti/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-simplicity.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~|simplicities}}

# The state or quality of being [[simple]]
## The quality or state of being [[unmixed]] or [[uncompounded]]
##: {{ux|en|as, the '''simplicity''' of metals or of earths}}
## The quality or state of being not [[complex]], or of consisting of few parts
##: {{ux|en|the '''simplicity''' of a machine}}
## Lack of [[sharpness]] of mind; lack of ability to think using complex ideas; [[stupidity]]
## Lack of artificial [[ornament]], pretentious style, or [[luxury]]; [[plainness]]
##: {{ux|en|'''simplicity''' of dress, of style, or of language}}
##: {{ux|en|'''simplicity''' of diet}}
##: {{ux|en|'''simplicity''' of life}}
## Freedom from [[subtlety]] or [[abstruseness]]; [[clarity]]
##: {{ux|en|the '''simplicity''' of a doctrine}}
##: {{ux|en|the '''simplicity''' of an explanation or a demonstration}}
## Freedom from [[complication]]; [[efficiency]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-08-03|volume=408|issue=8847|magazine={{w|The Economist}}
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21582498-america-has-changed-way-it-measures-gdp-boundary-problems Boundary problems]
|passage=Economics is a messy discipline: too fluid to be a science, too rigorous to be an art. Perhaps it is fitting that economists’ most-used metric, gross domestic product (GDP), is a tangle too. GDP measures the total value of output in an economic territory. Its apparent '''simplicity''' explains why it is scrutinised down to tenths of a percentage point every month.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|rare}} An act or instance of foolishness.
#* {{RQ:Florio Montaigne Essayes|chapter=31|book=II|passage=speaking of the great '''simplicity''' we commit, in leaving yong children under the government and charge of their fathers and parents.}}

